sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Holaspis22 cuticle Turing wavelength at 15 µm (Wenlock, 428.1 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg patch whose analytical wavelength is 15.14 µm (dispersion Pearson r = 0.99963, RMSE 0.03185). At fixed D_u, raising r = D_v/D_u from 8 to 60 shortens lambda_c monotonically from 15.94 µm to 14.82 µm and raises the peak growth rate; the pass-1 guess that lambda would lengthen was wrong for g_v < 0. Dropping the u^2 v coupling drops the amplitude ratio to 0.0033, against 0.0361 for equal diffusivities. The GIF last frame versus the pinned fossil: Sobel-orientation KS = 0.022 (L1 = 0.011), 24-bin radial FFT cosine = 0.9999, cv_sim_similarity = 96.0. Post-cephalic rib count on the photograph is 23.89 against the literature thoracic count of 22. Versus holaspis18, 1.115^4 = 1.546 entry-size ratio and 1.265 wavelengths per tergite at 15 µm. Overall 87.2/100 (faithfulness 87.0, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit bccebbf75b51e8bb043c3de77327726083ae28b8; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.18.1, pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0.py at bccebbf75b51e8bb043c3de77327726083ae28b8, image/gif, 3951972 B, 611×720 px, 14 frames, artifact_sha256 3284ad707b7efd78aef2da088279abd602641ebc3eea61d6ee0352cf80da551d (sha256 3284ad707b7efd78aef2da088279abd602641ebc3eea61d6ee0352cf80da551d), spec_fingerprint 47904938ec440c71d3ae9e4ad06d8226684eebc47ce74d3df60816aaa69afd77. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 47904938ec440c71d3ae9e4ad06d8226684eebc47ce74d3df60816aaa69afd77; artifact_sha256: 3284ad707b7efd78aef2da088279abd602641ebc3eea61d6ee0352cf80da551d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_specimen.jpg=1b6c8997dc42e91d..., datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=27a4d89f420f5947..., datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=18715738c9f9b9cc..., datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis22_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=05678f16da15a24f...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis22-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Five holaspid morphs with 18–22 thoracic segments; hemianamorphosis; precocious specification of the adult count (Fusco et al. 2004). | Meraspid per-stage growth 1.115 and holaspid per-stage growth 1.103; thoracic release ends at s18 for t18 and s22 for t22 (Hughes et al. 2017). | A shape transition near glabellar length 1.7 mm is not strictly tied to segment number (Hughes & Chapman 1995).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian and k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), with the length unit set so lambda_c = 1.514e-5 m. | Entry-size ratio 1.115^4 and the per-tergite wavelength-count ratio against the 18-segment predecessor. | Segment-accretion reveal on the pinned dorsal photograph, with the simulated activator painted into the two eye regions.; transfer_boundary: The catalog ages 428.3 Ma (holaspis18) and 428.1 Ma (holaspis22) are series bookkeeping. Fusco et al. 2004 describe contemporaneous intraspecific morphs from one narrow Wenlock interval near 429 Ma. | 15 µm is the assigned cellular detail scale for this slot. It is not a lens diameter measured on Aulacopleura.; does_not_claim: That the fossil photograph resolves 15 µm ocelli. | That 18- and 22-segment animals are successive chronospecies separated by 0.2 Myr. | That Schnakenberg kinetics were written down by Fusco, Hughes, or Turing; Turing 1952 supplies the dispersion relation, Schnakenberg supplies a two-species carrier that realizes it.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1 closed: at fixed D_u, r from 8 to 60 shortens lambda_c monotonically from 15.94 µm to 14.82 µm. Peak growth rate rises. Pass 1 expected lengthening; that sign is wrong for g_v < 0 and is corrected here.",
            "remediation needed: R2 closed: quadratic-coupling ablation amplitude ratio is 0.0033, beside the equal-diffusion control at 0.0361.",
            "remediation needed: R3 closed: specimen versus GIF last frame, KS = 0.022 on magnitude-weighted Sobel angles, orientation L1 = 0.011, 24-bin radial FFT cosine = 0.9999.",
            "remediation needed: R4 closed: the comparison figure reports Pearson r, RMSE, the diffusivity sweep, and the orientation histograms." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.872"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

